<main><article class="document"><div class="eyebrow">Model card · v0.2</div><h1>Intended use and limitations</h1><section><h2>Model purpose</h2><p>EventScape examines how recommendation objectives can interact with social exposure, participation, provider concentration, and network structure in synthetic environments.</p></section><section><h2>Intended users</h2><p>Computational social scientists, recommender-systems researchers, students, reviewers, and engineers auditing model assumptions.</p></section><section><h2>Valid uses</h2><ul><li>Reproducing canonical synthetic scenarios.</li><li>Comparing policy behavior under controlled parameters.</li><li>Testing software determinism and metric definitions.</li><li>Generating hypotheses for separately governed empirical research.</li></ul></section><section><h2>Invalid uses</h2><ul><li>Predicting behavior of a real community.</li><li>Inferring protected characteristics.</li><li>Choosing policies for deployment without empirical validation and governance.</li><li>Claiming causal social effects from the prepared demonstration.</li></ul></section><section><h2>Known limitations</h2><p>The model uses two synthetic groups, simplified interest and event supply, stylized attendance choice, and bounded network dynamics. Prepared outputs are exploratory demonstrations with eight matched seeds, not a preregistered powered study.</p></section><section><h2>Governance</h2><p>Changes to attendance equations, tie formation, primary metrics, random-number behavior, policy semantics, or reproduction manifests require a versioned decision record.</p></section></article></main><style>.document { max-width: 820px; padding: 5rem 0; }.document section { border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); padding: 2rem 0; } li { margin: .5rem 0; line-height: 1.5; }</style>
